  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets 55 °C testing and a 5% per-model benchmark, but exceeding it triggers only corrective action and retesting, with no sales stop; per-model rates go to buyers and existing customers but not the public, which protects Northwind's 6.2% flagship. S5 keeps a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which bites Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while S4's 36-month suppression start is acceptable and S3 allows an open-ended 'where technically feasible' 72-month retrofit. S1 reporting covers only serious incidents, with no deadline for other thermal events."
